    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0524" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/807.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 14, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President Nouel will resign early in April, if not sooner. His brother, the
                    Minister of the Interior, promises to give me the earliest information as to the
                    exact date. The President’s health is said to have improved slightly but the
                    doctors forbid his resuming work until after a complete rest. He is in Barahona
                    recuperating.</p>
                <p>All are aware of the approaching resignation and are preparing accordingly. Vidal
                    and Arias are supposedly working together. Vasquez is well prepared. Velasquez
                    is said to be the choice of Congress.</p>
                <p>At least one gunboat should be here all the time, not leaving for coal unless
                    replaced by another.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
